no":"","first":"István","key":"tarrósypedh","last":"Tarrósy","name":"Tarrósy, István","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1163/9789004734777_002","eisbn":["9789004734777"],"isbn":["9789004734760"],"pages":"1-16","place":"Leiden","publisher":"Brill","series":"AEGIS-Brill African Studies Series","status":"p","title":"Trust and Trust-Making in Africa’s Global Connections"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6f38fb63-2b8a-44d3-9d38-76b1c7af5f16"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introduction Trust and Trust-Making in Africa’s Global Connections : Reflections on Crisis and Collaboration","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829117","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"In this article we develop the concept of addressability to help us unpack processes of identification. We start from a foundational sociological account of addressing as laid out by Simmel, and use Luhmann’s systems theory to identify tensions in the overlap between different systems. The dual character of addressing as reductive (in meaning) and constructive (of communicative positions) helps us understand a mode of knowledge production that generates its own recipients. By concentrating on the moment of addressing in this manner and developing the concept of addressability to explain its complexity, we seek to build an analytic concept that is useful for scholars who are interested in unpacking the construction of communicative positions in identification. We demonstrate the potential of this concept with an analysis of two moments of addressability in action that involve personal identification numbers. We conclude that the intersection and mutual challenge of these two approaches can help us connect different addressing moments while also moving beyond questions of surveillance and entitlement that routinely seek to capture the problem of identification.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Cakici, Baki","Thiel, Alena"],"cuid":["S02-091.43-822883"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Identification","Surveillance","Systems theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"addressability i identification and communicative positions in critical sociological perspective i","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.37062/sf.62.27828","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.43-822883","identifier":[{"id":"105008954431","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f5fb7355-a893-46cb-9494-f6514318100b","ku-40601547-2182-419d-a44c-f771bc590b5c"],"keyword":["Addressability","Identification","Identification numbers","Surveillance","Systems theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B396EF3C666D4455A0F8785132098970"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.37062/sf.62.27828","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/461831411/07_SoFo_nr_1_2_2025_cakici_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, ETHOS Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","locid":"b614ac6f-eefa-44a3-8b9a-092b88d86d37","name":"Cakici, Baki","orcid":"0000-0002-1039-8177","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"f240d002-893f-45bd-b9ad-6a6ddc015e40","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.37062/sf.62.27828","issn":["00380342"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"Sociologisk Forskning","pages":"107-120","status":"p","title":"Sociologisk Forskning","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008954431"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f5fb7355-a893-46cb-9494-f6514318100b","ku-40601547-2182-419d-a44c-f771bc590b5c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Addressability: Identification and Communicative Positions in Critical Sociological Perspective","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.43-822883","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Since Ghana's return to democratic rule in 1992, the West African country has recurrently been heralded as the model for democracy in Africa. Despite multiple controversies challenging core democratic institutions, Ghana's 2024 elections again represent a strong indicator of the country's democratic resilience. Combining our multi-disciplinary perspectives, we identify the key concerns that preoccupied Ghanaian voters in the lead-up to election day on 7 December 2024. We argue that there is a disconnect between campaign promises, such as the transition into a digital economy, and Ghanaians’ existential worries about the future. Concerns about both environmental and economic liveability equally informed the voter migration behind the 2024 election's unusually large margin of victory. Debates around the alignment of both flagbearers with Ghana's major religious groups, alongside Ghanaians’ rejection of the dismantling of democratic institutions, indicate that Ghana's new government will have to live up to voters’ demands for authenticity and accountability.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena","Lauterbach, Karen","Agyekum, Humphrey Asamoah","Bob-Milliar, George"],"cuid":["S02-085.71-813960"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Ghana"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kwame Nkrumah University"],"keyword":["Digitalisation","Elections","Galamsey","Ghana","Religion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ghana s 000000002024 elections ghanaians vote for renewal and accountability","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/00020397251352867","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-085.71-813960","ids":["itu-98dcf57a-782a-4293-a23c-2a61d02ce0ad","ku-340ba31d-808f-45b9-a6b2-aed050af33eb"],"keyword":["Democratic resilience","Digitalisation","Elections","Galamsey","Ghana","Religion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9FAC1623F82F44B0AF77186E94188035"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/00020397251352867","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/458176037/agyekum-et-al-2025-ghana-s-2024-elections-ghanaians-vote-for-renewal-and-accountability.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, ETHOS Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gh","key":"kwame nkrumah university","loc":["Ghana","Africa"],"name":"Kwame Nkrumah University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"f240d002-893f-45bd-b9ad-6a6ddc015e40","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Humphrey Asamoah","key":"agyekumpau","last":"Agyekum","locid":"c8a940ce-c38f-4ef0-bb0a-dded3c8486a8","name":"Agyekum, Humphrey Asamoah","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"George M.","key":"bobmilliarpau","last":"Bob-Milliar","locid":"8f15d111-537f-4eee-ac30-de234f03d2a9","name":"Bob-Milliar, George M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Karen","key":"lauterbachpau","last":"Lauterbach","locid":"d81f6ad6-0598-47d9-af50-3137fb9c6118","name":"Lauterbach, Karen","orcid":"0000-0003-4962-3383","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/00020397251352867","issn":["00020397","18686869"],"issn_org":["00020397"],"issue":"2","journal":"Africa Spectrum","pages":"209-220","status":"p","title":"Africa Spectrum","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-98dcf57a-782a-4293-a23c-2a61d02ce0ad","ku-340ba31d-808f-45b9-a6b2-aed050af33eb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ghana's 2024 Elections: Ghanaians Vote for Renewal and Accountability","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.71-813960","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Trust and Trust-Making in Africa’s Global Connections is a thought-provoking book contributing to both African Studies and the study of trust in society. The volume provides rich ethnographic insights into the ways trust and trust-making shape Africans’ global encounters. It traces empirical foundations of trust and distrust, illustrates the wide variation in manifestations of trust-building, and critically positions these observations in the contemporary moment of global polycrisis. Trust and trust-making, we show, as these critically engage with global power relations, are acting both as a catalyst of harm and a potential source of positive change.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena","Kaag, Mayke","Tarrosy, Istvan"],"cuid":["S02-088.00-822870"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Hungary","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leiden University","University of Amsterdam","University of Pécs"],"keyword":["African Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trust and trust making in africa s global connections","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://brill.com/display/title/72508","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-088.00-822870","ids":["itu-68554e49-e3dd-4fcb-ba77-e6760e55ec4d","ku-8eff158d-1560-4bfa-801c-f4b4e07f69a5"],"keyword":["African Studies","Ethnographic Insights","Global Connections","Global Power Relations","Trust-making"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-B8C6653EDA9FD825A8C0E38E32C9B724"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"it