{"abstract":"This chapter presents the history of the population census in the West African country of Ghana. Combining archival with qualitative interviews, research for this chapter traced the Ghanaian census history from its colonial past to current ambitions of developing new measurement practices based on interoperability-based population data infrastructures. Approaching Ghana’s census history from the point of view of the method and infrastructural innovations – that is, the arrangements of devices, software, experts, and organizational knowledge – and their global circulations, the paper explores how quantitative methods run through societal and political transformations as forces of stabilization. Following Didier, these “marbling veins” of census and statistical conventions run through the bedrock of society, thus allowing to shed new light on the political transformations that have shaped Ghana’s history since the mid-19th century. Particular attention will be paid to changing quantitative forms in relation to nation-building, from the first post-independence enumeration in light of Pan-Africanist ideology to the recent contestations around identity and technology in Africa.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-829762"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"techno political transformation and adaptability in ghanaian census history","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4324/9781003259749-15","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-829762","identifier":[{"id":"85191242246","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bcf66ae7-6676-432b-b985-bb847fc8322b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D717C68321E425775ED6E5DE8FAFF085"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/461842932/Techno-political_transformation_and_adaptability_in_Ghanaian_census_history_25_09_01_13_36_39.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4324/9781003259749-15","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"8eaf409f-f6a1-439e-a8e1-c7c1da0c88da","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Walter","key":"bartlpedh","last":"Bartl","name":"Bartl, Walter","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"suterpedh","last":"Suter","name":"Suter, Christian","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alberto","key":"veiraramospedh","last":"Veira-Ramos","name":"Veira-Ramos, Alberto","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4324/9781003259749-15","eisbn":["9781003259749"],"pages":"283-302","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","subtitle":"Quantifying Populations, Institutional Autonomy, Innovation","title":"The Global Politics of Census Taking"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bcf66ae7-6676-432b-b985-bb847fc8322b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Techno-political transformation and adaptability in Ghanaian census history","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829762","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Biometric identification technologies have been heralded by development practitioners, state bureaucrats, the biometric industry, and technology enthusiasts alike as a means to increase accountability and transparency, while reducing discretion in bureaucratic encounters. However, the proliferation of biometric technologies in Ghana since the early 2010s, has increasingly rendered the exchange of credentials for the purpose of establishing unique identities invisible, retreating thus into the background of person-to-person, person-to-business, and state-citizen interactions. Drawing on the case of Ghana, the chapter presents contemporary innovations in identity registration and the ways in which these have altered the production of personhood. Explicit attention will be paid to the processes “making up” personhood in relation to datafied selves and the technologies co-producing them. It will be argued that the immersion of identification technologies into the lifeworld, as a moment of technicisation, is necessarily incomplete. This is because data frictions bring into focus the moment of classification, including the haunting of hegemonic categories. These frictions produce an oscillation between immersion and detachment from the lifeworld, which can provide a potential starting point for the critique of postcolonial data politics in Ghana.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789576"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biometric data doubles and the technicisation of personhood in ghana","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1163/9789004688285_008","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789576","identifier":[{"id":"85205536557","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e25e02c1-6a02-49f6-a4d7-f7fd15fc57d9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-DF88472D627D5F3D9C9819A63C9C5749"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1163/9789004688285_008","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://brill.com/downloadpdf/display/book/9789004688285/BP000015.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"f240d002-893f-45bd-b9ad-6a6ddc015e40","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Richard","key":"rottenburgpedh","last":"Rottenburg","name":"Rottenburg, Richard","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"riedkepedh","last":"Riedke","name":"Riedke, Eva","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1163/9789004688285_008","eisbn":["9789004688285"],"pages":"150-170","place":"Leiden: Brill","status":"p","title":"Translating Technology in Africa: Technicisation","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205536557"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e25e02c1-6a02-49f6-a4d7-f7fd15fc57d9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Biometric Data Doubles and the Technicisation of Personhood in Ghana","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789576","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
