{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Agyekum, Humphrey Asamoah"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754791"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mental health in ghana standardisation advocacy and changing perceptions of care and disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-754791","identifier":[{"id":"105005683902","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b5899074-174a-4e85-b16e-a15143d1766c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-5-6-13BACB14FDCF6D91C7254D672639076E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology, Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Humphrey Asamoah","key":"agyekumpau","last":"Agyekum","locid":"c8a940ce-c38f-4ef0-bb0a-dded3c8486a8","name":"Agyekum, Humphrey Asamoah","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alena","key":"thielpedh","last":"Thiel","name":"Thiel, Alena","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Samuel Aniegye","key":"ntewusupedh","last":"Ntewusu","name":"Ntewusu, Samuel Aniegye","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-981-97-3500-6","pages":"67-89","place":"Singapore","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","subtitle":"Health Records and Knowledge Production in Ghana","title":"The Social Life of Health Data"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b5899074-174a-4e85-b16e-a15143d1766c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mental Health in Ghana : Standardisation, Advocacy and Changing Perceptions of Care and Disease","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754791","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"How can we make good decisions in contexts of radical uncertainty? Over the last years, Ghana has been the scene of numerous disasters, both anthropogenic and naturally occurring. Recent incidences range from the Apeatse gas explosion in January 2022, to recurrent devastating flooding, and the outbreak of infectious diseases. Among its key priorities of action, the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction (SFDRR, 2015-2030) proposes substantive investments in knowledge about disaster risks, resilience and disaster preparedness. With the mid-term review of the SFDRR in 2023, knowledge infrastructures, data capacities and collaboration with statistical communities for the anticipatory analysis of disaster risks have again received top-level attention. So far, however, African implementation of the SFDRR has remained focused on reactive rather than preventive action (Bang et al. 2019). The paper illuminates Ghanaian DRR experts' creative data practices as vital elements in the country's ability to effectively respond to extreme vulnerability.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695225"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data practices","Decision making","Disaster Risk Reduction","Radical Uncertainty","Sendai Framework"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data innovation for disaster risk reduction in ghana","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-695225","ids":["itu-1a9c3380-6349-412b-bc0b-671f3b5fcccd"],"keyword":["Data Practices","Decision Making","Disaster Risk Reduction","Radical Uncertainty","Sendai Framework"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-20387381F54DD984D96F806674DC2C72"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"f240d002-893f-45bd-b9ad-6a6ddc015e40","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1a9c3380-6349-412b-bc0b-671f3b5fcccd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Data Innovation for Disaster Risk Reduction in Ghana","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695225","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Around the globe, the Covid-19 pandemic generated uncertainties in relation to the novel virus itself, its treatment and its socio-economic effects on an international scale. In addition, various claims of truth about the pandemic added to the situation’s complexity. In this article, we analyse Ghana’s initial response to Covid-19 to illustrate how complex assemblages of political elites and knowledge production infrastructures intersected in the pursuit of capturing knowledge about an unfolding crisis. With the critical function of knowledge production about the pandemic as a lens, this article narrows in on Ghana’s crisis response and the composition of the contemporary Ghanaian political landscape it revealed, particularly in relation to declining trust in policies and State institutions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena","Agyekum, Humphrey"],"cuid":["S02-089.29-686178"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Covid 19","Ghana","Imposition of Restriction Act","Surveillant assemblage"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crisis politics and the 000000002020 imposition of restrictions act in ghana","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-089.29-686178","identifier":[{"id":"85165301004","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-eed29187-3bb0-4add-b158-a983c87b447f","ku-5602ebba-abaa-46dc-bda6-0e50a185ca8f"],"keyword":["Covid-19","Ghana","Imposition of Restriction Act","Surveillant assemblage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-6F2EC996CABED43BB00E2A5CBD3A38A8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2026-01-01","type":"rem","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"8eaf409f-f6a1-439e-a8e1-c7c1da0c88da","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Humphrey","key":"agyekumpau","last":"Agyekum","locid":"40fe53e5-4832-4ddb-8935-61badeb7962c","name":"Agyekum, Humphrey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4000/etudesafricaines.41846","issn":["00080055","17775353"],"issn_org":["00080055"],"journal":"Cahiers d'Etudes Africaines","pages":"363-383","status":"p","title":"Cahiers d'Etudes Africaines","volume":"252"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published","Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-eed29187-3bb0-4add-b158-a983c87b447f","ku-5602ebba-abaa-46dc-bda6-0e50a185ca8f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Crisis Politics and the 2020 “Imposition of Restrictions Act” in Ghana","type":"Journal Article","url":"https:/