{"abstract":"This contribution focuses on the recent introduction of a digital addressing system in Ghana. Initially developed in the slipstream of the restructuring of the Ghana Post, the oldest public service institution in the country, the digital addressing system has recently been tied into the country's broader digital identification agenda. The article examines how innovations in geospatial (population) data infrastructure alter the Ghanaian state's view on the spatial distribution of the population as well as on individuals by associating them within certain spatial categories, and eventually, (re)formatting the way in which the national space is produced and disciplined. In view of the limitations of earlier paper-based registers, particular attention is paid to the integration of various population registers thus afforded.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena"],"cuid":["S02-091.43-686172"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Digital addressing","Digital identification","Ghana","Interoperability","Postal reform"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital addressing and the construction of the ghanaian nation space","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diggeo.2023.100054","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.43-686172","identifier":[{"id":"85149772240","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6774701c-c698-4c22-a050-8e941f08d77a","ku-b862a659-2947-40cd-99df-0c720507a737"],"keyword":["Digital addressing","Digital identification","Ghana","Interoperability","Postal reform"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-B49DDB037F1ECB95F9B7B627C22047DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2666378323000065","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diggeo.2023.100054","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2666378323000065/pdfft?md5=e7ae1e0cce3f2ad3cbda7f1a135369c1&pid=1-s2.0-S2666378323000065-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/339850847/Digital_addressing_and_the_construction_of_the_Gha_2023_Digital_Geography_an.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, The Study Board at African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"8eaf409f-f6a1-439e-a8e1-c7c1da0c88da","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.diggeo.2023.100054","issn":["26663783"],"journal":"Digital Geography and Society","paperid":"100054","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Digital Geography and Society","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6774701c-c698-4c22-a050-8e941f08d77a","ku-b862a659-2947-40cd-99df-0c720507a737"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digital addressing and the construction of the Ghanaian nation-space","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.43-686172","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This article studies population censuses in colonial and post-colonial Ghana by showing the inflections and developments that quantification tools have undergone there. The history of quantification, as shown by Emmanuel Didier in 2021, provides useful insight into the study of the transformation of society because it is consubstantial with the very foundation of society. Thus, it has long been thought that these quantification processes jointly participated in the constitution of different types of \"data subjects\", individuals as they are identified by means of data according to the definition given by Evelyn Ruppert in 2008. This article explores the limits within which the concept of \"data subjects\" applies to the postcolonial context. It pays particular attention to the need for reorganization imposed by technological developments and to the constant resistance to the colonizing power of the datafication process.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689176"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ghana","Ghana Statistical Service","census history","data subjects","population and housing Census"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"une histoire politique du recensement au ghana aux 000000000020e et 000000000021e siècles","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://publications-sfds.fr/index.php/stat_soc/article/view/845","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-689176","ids":["itu-0f71f7f7-3ed0-403a-8ed2-9aed319d2bf3"],"keyword":["Ghana","Ghana Statistical Service","census history","data subjects","population and housing Census"],"lang":"French","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-37F41A0729D569FCCBBEAAFB6E7BE8EC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://publications-sfds.fr/index.php/stat_soc/article/view/845","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"f240d002-893f-45bd-b9ad-6a6ddc015e40","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["22690271"],"issue":"1","journal":"Statistique et Société","pages":"59-78","status":"p","title":"Statistique et Société","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0f71f7f7-3ed0-403a-8ed2-9aed319d2bf3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Une histoire politique du recensement au Ghana aux 20e et 21e siècles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689176","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This article proposes a comparative socio-economic history of quantification in Ecuador, Brazil, Ghana and Sierra Leone. It narrows in on censuses in the Global South as sites of methodological and infrastructural innovation in the context of global circulations of model population data systems, methodological standards, and material infrastructures. Specifically, the authors ask which arrangements of actors, norms and settings are involved in the reception, translation and adaptation of statistical innovation and how uneven relations and compositions of power between and within these fields shape the process of transmission. Distilling from their explorative, hermeneutic approach, the authors explore the mechanisms that link variously positioned political fields (Bourdieu, 1985) in the production and implementation of statistical innovation in the Global South. Four mechanisms are identified that shape statistical innovation as process of reception of globally circulating models and ideas as well as their adaptations into specific fields, all of which have differentiated effects and play under certain conditions in parallel or combined ways: 1) interventionist impulses from international organizations, 2) commercial and institutional brokerage, 3) initiatives from local professional communities, and 4) effects of political instabilities.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena","Villacis, Byron","Capistrano, Daniel","Carvalho da Silva, Christyne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689199"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","Ireland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Institute of Educational Studies and Investigations Brasília","University College Dublin","University of California"],"keyword":["Brazil","Digitalization","Ecuador","Ghana","Sierra Leone","Statistical innovation","Translation","population censuses"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"statistical innovation in the global south mechanisms of translation in censuses of brazil ecuador ghana and sierra leone","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102685318/Statistical_innovation_in_the_Global_South.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-689199","identifier":[{"id":"85139409491","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e92895c1-4d34-4c91-bbf3-857598d98df1"],"keyword":["Brazil","Ecuador","Ghana","Sierra Leone","Statistical innovation","digitalization","population censuses","translation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7536AA556335BD3D49D4ED06E8D9ECFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102685318/Statistical_innovation_in_the_Global_South.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ie","key":"university college dublin","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University College Dublin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"br","key":"national institute of educational studies and investigations brasília","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"National Institute of Educational Studies and Investigations Brasília","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"f240d002-893f-45bd-b9ad-6a6ddc015e40","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Byron","key":"villacispau","last":"Villacis","name":"Villacis, Byron","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"capistranopau","last":"Capistrano","name":"Capistrano, Daniel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christyne","key":"carvalhodasilvapau","last":"Carvalho da Silva","name":"Carvalho da Silva, Christyne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1163/15691330-bja10060","issn":["15691322","15691330"],"issn_org":["15691322"],"issue":"4","journal":"Comparative Sociology","pages":"419-446","publisher":"Brill Academic Publishers","status":"p","title":"Comparative Sociology","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e92895c1-4d34-4c91-bbf3-857598d98df1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Statistical Innovation in the Global South : Mechanisms of Translation in Censuses of Brazil, Ecuador, Ghana and Sierra Leone","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689199","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
