{"abstract":"Biometric identity registration technologies are spreading throughout the world. Developing countries in particular, have recently been seen to construct biometric population registers in partnership with international donor organizations. This article traces the temporal entanglements produced by transnational policy mobilities in the inception and implementation of Ghana's national biometric identity registration project. In 2008, Ghana famously introduced the first biometric banking system in Africa. Yet, the e-zwich payment system marked only the first step towards the current ‘craze’ for biometric identity registration in the West African country. Among the numerous biometric identity documents circulating in Ghana's national and subnational institutions, the national Ghanacard is the most interesting identity registration project in the country, both in terms of its population-wide reach and the complex constellation of institutions, actors and ideas competing within the project. With a focus on the temporalities of policymaking, the article examines the project's fundamental future orientation, the temporal context of its production with its specific possibilities of imagining and acting upon certain matters, and the rhythms and schedules of project implementation. By doing so, it draws attention to some of the ways in which competing sets of ideas shape large-scale investments in technology and infrastructure in Africa.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689192"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biometric Identity Registration","Ghanacard","Technological Infrastructure Investment","Temporalities of Policymaking","Transnational Policy Mobilities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"entangled temporalities ghana s national biometric identity registration project","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1467-8322.12321","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-689192","identifier":[{"id":"85011333329","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-85e1d009-f813-43e7-b81d-8565675ec91e"],"keyword":["Biometric Identity Registration","Ghanacard","Technological Infrastructure Investment","Temporalities of Policymaking","Transnational Policy Mobilities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F6645E1E8CE4907A9A65A298A582C42A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1467-8322.12321","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"f240d002-893f-45bd-b9ad-6a6ddc015e40","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1467-8322.12321","issn":["0268540X","14678322"],"issue":"5","journal":"Anthropology Today","pages":"3-5","status":"p","title":"Anthropology Today","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-85e1d009-f813-43e7-b81d-8565675ec91e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Entangled temporalities: Ghana's national biometric identity registration project","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/