{"abstract":"It is impossible to understand the gendered relation between women and public space without taking into account its other, that is, male engagements with and in space. Our joint paper contrasts the public spaces of a market and a bus station in central Accra, Ghana. While the former is historically associated with female entrepreneurship, masculinity is deeply inscribed in the activities defining the latter. However, recent developments gradually undermine these gendered divides. By focusing on interpersonal claims to entrepreneurial places in the two locations, we illustrate how the configurations and co-constructions of gender and space are exposed to on-going, often subtle shifts, which are impelled by dialectically grounded transformations of quotidian spatial practices and social relations. Expanding upon the notion of viri–/uxorilocality, we explore shifts in the gendered strategies of newcomers establishing their presence in the two spaces and the extent to which these practices may alter gendered spatial significations.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena","Stasik, Michael"],"cuid":["S02-086.11-686174"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bayreuth"],"keyword":["Accra","Gender","Ghana","Markets","bus stations","place space"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"market men and station women changing significations of gendered space in accra ghana","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02589001.2017.1281385","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.11-686174","identifier":[{"id":"85011600812","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8e8707c3-d0fa-47c3-ac9f-3cc0b40c380b","ku-658e69a4-0719-4521-97c4-8d19413584fc"],"keyword":["Accra","Gender","Ghana","bus stations","markets","place/space"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-2F5DB01918DC50AE7F1195E65F300FE5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02589001.2017.1281385","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of bayreuth","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bayreuth","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"8eaf409f-f6a1-439e-a8e1-c7c1da0c88da","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"stasikpau","last":"Stasik","name":"Stasik, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/02589001.2017.1281385","issn":["02589001","14699397"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Contemporary African Studies","pages":"459-478","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Journal of Contemporary African Studies","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8e8707c3-d0fa-47c3-ac9f-3cc0b40c380b","ku-658e69a4-0719-4521-97c4-8d19413584fc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Market men and station women : Changing significations of gendered space in Accra, Ghana","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.11-686174","year":2016,"yearsub":2016}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena"],"cuid":["S02-096.30-822874"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"imaginaires d authenticité et leurs négociations dans le marché de marchandises de chine à accra","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-096.30-822874","ids":["itu-6ad4c116-4ba6-4e39-8221-b8dcee0c791e","ku-a638c5d5-37d1-44af-b88a-0ed5254c0f42"],"lang":"French","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-99DC6F8560B043EA1AD163A17CFC0FA1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, The Study Board at African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"8eaf409f-f6a1-439e-a8e1-c7c1da0c88da","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"345-370","place":"Paris","publisher":"Karthala","status":"p","title":"Entrepreneurs africains et chinois: Les impacts sociaux d’une rencontre particulière"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6ad4c116-4ba6-4e39-8221-b8dcee0c791e","ku-a638c5d5-37d1-44af-b88a-0ed5254c0f42"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Imaginaires d’authenticité et leurs négociations dans le marché de marchandises de Chine à Accra","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.30-822874","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Drawing on theories of networked socio-economic life in West Africa, we advance that the types of Ghanaian and Senegalese communities’ social organization in Yiwu, Guangzhou and Hong Kong have important effects on their members’ entrepreneurial success and upward social mobility. We argue that as an expression of “vernacular cosmopolitanism” (Appiah 1998, Diouf 2000), the circulation of capitals, for example between stablished entrepreneurs and newcomers, is controlled by distinct yet mutually integrated networks. While “networks of accumulation” (Meagher 2006, 2010) give preferential treatment to kin – and community –mediated relations, “networks of survival” lack such strong expressions of solidarity. Here, structural factors external to communal life may allow a newcomer to advance in the career and eventually penetrate into a network of accumulation”, in which insights and experiences but also functional contacts with the Chinese business and bureaucratic channels are concentrated. In their capacity to mobilize the spheres of influence they reach into – be it for members of their network or sporadically also the compatriot in urgent need - “networks of accumulation” of Ghanaian and Senegalese agents in China overlap decisively with the process of community formation","author_count":2,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena","Marfaing, Laurence"],"cuid":["S02-099.54-822875"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Institute of Global and Area Studies"],"keyword":["Community formation","Entrepreneurial success","Networked socio economic life","Networks of accumulation","Vernacular cosmopolitanism"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"networks spheres of influence and the mediation of opportunity the case of west african trade agents in china","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-099.54-822875","ids":["itu-6b862639-1d44-4a80-9027-a79a6b80a7bb","ku-dad4c57f-04b6-44a4-bbc2-4647af2a4c6e"],"keyword":["Community formation","Entrepreneurial success","Networked socio-economic life","Networks of accumulation","Vernacular cosmopolitanism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-43F4C61A72A1F3A058A41B676F09B8D2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"german institute of global and area studies","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Institute of Global and Area Studies","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"8eaf409f-f6a1-439e-a8e1-c7c1da0c88da","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurence","key":"marfaingpau","last":"Marfaing","name":"Marfaing, Laurence","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19426569"],"issue":"10","journal":"Africology: The Journal of Pan-African Studies","pages":"65-84","status":"p","title":"Africology: The Journal of Pan-African Studies","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6b862639-1d44-4a80-9027-a79a6b80a7bb","ku-dad4c57f-04b6-44a4-bbc2-4647af2a4c6e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Networks, spheres of influence and the mediation of opportunity: The case of West African trade agents in China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.54-822875","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
